IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `br-core`

-- br-core-tests-prazo.l4 -- tests of the time-limit and date rules of br-core.l4.
--
-- Every expected value below was worked out by hand from the calendar, not read from the output.
-- Where the calendar is not enough and a counting CONVENTION decides the answer, the test says so:
-- those are NOTES.md F1 (the event day is day 0, the last day is still in time) and
-- F2 (months and years stop at the last day of a shorter month). The Law itself has no counting rule.
-- Dates are built with YMD, which is checked first against the built-in DATE_YEAR, DATE_MONTH and DATE_DAY.

§ `br-core tests 1: YMD`

-- The enactment date of the Law (title block, line 5: "LEI No 6.404, DE 15 DE DEZEMBRO DE 1976").
#ASSERT DATE_YEAR (YearMonthDay 1976 12 15) EQUALS 1976
#ASSERT DATE_MONTH (YearMonthDay 1976 12 15) EQUALS 12
#ASSERT DATE_DAY (YearMonthDay 1976 12 15) EQUALS 15

-- Year first: a transposed call does not mean the same date.
#ASSERT NOT (YearMonthDay 2026 1 10 EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 10 1)

-- Inherited leniency (F2): an impossible day rolls into the next month and nothing is reported.
-- 2023 is not a leap year, so 29 February 2023 is 1 March 2023.
#ASSERT YearMonthDay 2023 2 29 EQUALS YearMonthDay 2023 3 1

§ `br-core tests 2: o termo final do prazo, em dias`

-- Art. 137, IV: 30 days from publication. April has 30 days, so 10 April + 30 = 10 May.
#ASSERT `o termo final do prazo` (YearMonthDay 2026 4 10) (`prazo em dias` 30) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 5 10

-- February 2026 has 28 days: 20 February + 10 days = 2 March (8 days to 28 February, then 2 more).
#ASSERT `o termo final do prazo` (YearMonthDay 2026 2 20) (`prazo em dias` 10) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 3 2

-- February 2024 has 29 days: 20 February + 10 days = 1 March (9 days to 29 February, then 1 more).
#ASSERT `o termo final do prazo` (YearMonthDay 2024 2 20) (`prazo em dias` 10) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2024 3 1

-- Across the year end.
#ASSERT `o termo final do prazo` (YearMonthDay 2025 12 31) (`prazo em dias` 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 1 1

-- F1: a limit of zero days ends on the event day itself.
#ASSERT `o termo final do prazo` (YearMonthDay 2026 4 10) (`prazo em dias` 0) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 4 10

§ `br-core tests 3: o termo final do prazo, em meses e anos`

-- Art. 81, parágrafo único: 6 months from the deposit.
#ASSERT `o termo final do prazo` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 15) (`prazo em meses` 6) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 7 15

-- Across the year end: November + 3 months.
#ASSERT `o termo final do prazo` (YearMonthDay 2025 11 20) (`prazo em meses` 3) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 2 20

-- Art. 108, parágrafo único: 2 years from the transfer of the shares.
#ASSERT `o termo final do prazo` (YearMonthDay 2024 3 10) (`prazo em anos` 2) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 3 10

-- F2, CONVENTION and not calendar fact: 31 August + 6 months has no 31 February; the date stops at
-- the last day of February 2027 (28 days).
#ASSERT `o termo final do prazo` (YearMonthDay 2026 8 31) (`prazo em meses` 6) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2027 2 28

-- F2, CONVENTION: 29 February 2024 + 1 year has no 29 February 2025; it stops at 28 February.
#ASSERT `o termo final do prazo` (YearMonthDay 2024 2 29) (`prazo em anos` 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2025 2 28

§ `br-core tests 4: o ato foi praticado dentro do prazo`

-- Art. 137, IV: the reimbursement must be claimed within 30 days of publication of the minutes.
-- Published 10 April 2026, so the last day in time is 10 May 2026.
#ASSERT `o ato foi praticado dentro do prazo` (YearMonthDay 2026 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2026 4 10) (`prazo em dias` 30)
#ASSERT NOT (`o ato foi praticado dentro do prazo` (YearMonthDay 2026 5 11) (YearMonthDay 2026 4 10) (`prazo em dias` 30))

-- Done on the start date itself is in time (F1, day 0).
#ASSERT `o ato foi praticado dentro do prazo` (YearMonthDay 2026 4 10) (YearMonthDay 2026 4 10) (`prazo em dias` 30)

-- Done the day before the start date is not in time: it is early, not late.
#ASSERT NOT (`o ato foi praticado dentro do prazo` (YearMonthDay 2026 4 9) (YearMonthDay 2026 4 10) (`prazo em dias` 30))

-- Art. 108, parágrafo único: 2 years from a transfer on 10 March 2024.
#ASSERT `o ato foi praticado dentro do prazo` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2024 3 10) (`prazo em anos` 2)
#ASSERT NOT (`o ato foi praticado dentro do prazo` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 11) (YearMonthDay 2024 3 10) (`prazo em anos` 2))

§ `br-core tests 5: a data limite de antecedência`

-- Art. 124, § 1º, II: 21 days of notice before a meeting on 30 April 2026; 30 - 21 = 9 April.
#ASSERT `a data limite de antecedência` (YearMonthDay 2026 4 30) (`prazo em dias` 21) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 4 9

-- Backwards across a month end: 5 days before 3 March 2026 is 26 February (28-day February).
#ASSERT `a data limite de antecedência` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 3) (`prazo em dias` 5) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 2 26

-- One month before 15 May 2026.
#ASSERT `a data limite de antecedência` (YearMonthDay 2026 5 15) (`prazo em meses` 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 4 15

-- One year before 1 March 2026.
#ASSERT `a data limite de antecedência` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (`prazo em anos` 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2025 3 1

-- F2, CONVENTION: one month before 31 March 2026 stops at the last day of February (28 days).
#ASSERT `a data limite de antecedência` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 31) (`prazo em meses` 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 2 28

§ `br-core tests 6: o ato respeitou a antecedência`

-- A notice on 9 April for a meeting on 30 April leaves 21 days: enough.
#ASSERT `o ato respeitou a antecedência` (YearMonthDay 2026 4 9) (YearMonthDay 2026 4 30) (`prazo em dias` 21)

-- A notice on 10 April leaves 20 days: too late.
#ASSERT NOT (`o ato respeitou a antecedência` (YearMonthDay 2026 4 10) (YearMonthDay 2026 4 30) (`prazo em dias` 21))

-- A notice a month earlier is also enough.
#ASSERT `o ato respeitou a antecedência` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 4 30) (`prazo em dias` 21)
